WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.749 --> 00:00:06.922
This is the course library: every assigned source in one place, ready to open online.

2
00:00:06.922 --> 00:00:16.090
Browse or filter to find a source. Filter by week or by topic. Each card shows the core idea, the format, and where the source lives.

3
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:27.092
Open the full text. The red button on each card opens the reading, video, or audio in a new tab, on Blackboard, in open access, or on the official site. This site never hosts the reading itself.

4
00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:38.100
Open a source's detail page. It shows the abstract, the core idea, roughly how long the source takes, and an evidence profile: what the source studied and what it does not prove.

5
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:49.103
Use Source Practice on sources you have read. Source Practice in the sidebar gives each source guided questions and a read-out of what landed, so you know whether the reading actually stuck.

6
00:00:49.103 --> 00:00:56.267
Send sources to Compare. The Compare button on a detail page adds the source to your comparison tray.

7
00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:59.182
Source Practice is never scored.

8
00:00:59.182 --> 00:01:05.415
Where next: Take two or three sources into Compare Sources and hold them side by side.
